# pattern-data-model

## Pattern Data Structures

Pattern data consists of:
- 3D vectors (position, orientation) representing quantum states
- Coherence value [0.0-1.0] indicating pattern stability
- Generation count tracking evolutionary history
- Relationships to other patterns via DAG structure 

## Memory Tier System

Patterns exist in a three-tier memory architecture:
- Short-Term Memory (STM): New patterns, coherence >= 0.2
- Medium-Term Memory (MTM): Stable patterns, coherence >= 0.5
- Long-Term Memory (LTM): Highly stable patterns, coherence >= 0.8

Key files:
- src/memory/dothis.md
- src/quantum/quantum_processor.cpp

## Coherence Metrics

Pattern coherence calculation:
- Base coherence from spatial position/orientation
- Stability multiplier based on generation count
- Context score from related pattern coherence
- Time-based decay rate of 0.02 per cycle

Coherence thresholds:
- Below 0.2: Pattern considered unstable
- 0.2-0.5: STM stability range
- 0.5-0.8: MTM stability range 
- Above 0.8: LTM stability achieved

## Pattern Evolution

Evolution mechanics:
- Mutation rate inversely proportional to stability
- Parent-child relationships tracked in DAG
- Coherence inheritance through quantum entanglement
- Phase correlation calculations for related patterns

Key components:
- src/quantum/evolution.cpp
- include/quantum/pattern_evolution.h

## Pattern Relationships

Relationship types:
- Direct parent-child through evolution
- Spatial proximity in quantum manifold
- Coherence similarity (within 0.1 threshold)
- Entanglement strength above 0.6

Managed through:
- Directed acyclic graph (DAG) structure
- Relationship pruning below coherence threshold
- Automatic relationship formation based on proximity
- Hierarchical organization in memory tiers

